You can sit over here

293
00:12:35,951 --> 00:12:36,550
and work,

294
00:12:36,551 --> 00:12:37,450
and then you casually

295
00:12:37,451 --> 00:12:38,750
and handsomely turn around. Right.

296
00:12:47,150 --> 00:12:49,050
His eyes were misty.

297
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:50,300
Disgusting.

298
00:12:53,650 --> 00:12:55,008
Here come the fish-counters.

299
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:57,000
It suddenly came to me.

300
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:58,900
Shen Teng,

301
00:12:58,901 --> 00:13:00,300
come and sit.

302
00:13:00,301 --> 00:13:01,350
How's your eyesight?

303
00:13:03,450 --> 00:13:04,700
Just so so.

304
00:13:04,701 --> 00:13:05,500
Okay.

305
00:13:05,501 --> 00:13:06,450
What about memory?

306
00:13:06,451 --> 00:13:07,500
Even worse.

307
00:13:07,501 --> 00:13:08,800
Eyesight is better.

308
00:13:08,801 --> 00:13:09,800
Okay.

309
00:13:09,801 --> 00:13:11,050
I was looking for someone

310
00:13:11,051 --> 00:13:12,050
who has a bad eyesight and memory.

311
00:13:13,150 --> 00:13:14,050
That's you!

312
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:15,300
Mary.

313
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:19,300
How's your eyesight?

314
00:13:19,301 --> 00:13:19,900
Pretty good.

315
00:13:19,901 --> 00:13:20,400
Okay.

316
00:13:20,401 --> 00:13:21,500
How about your memory?

317
00:13:21,501 --> 00:13:22,650
Excellent.

318
00:13:22,651 --> 00:13:23,050
Good.

319
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:26,304
You can just

320
00:13:26,304 --> 00:13:27,900
make up a team.

321
00:13:29,700 --> 00:13:30,150
What team?

322
00:13:30,151 --> 00:13:32,200
It's called "we count each other".

323
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:34,050
Shen Ma Team.

324
00:13:34,051 --> 00:13:34,900
You can call it like this.

325
00:13:34,901 --> 00:13:35,650
Why?

326
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:37,792
Because you are counting fish later.

327
00:13:37,984 --> 00:13:38,550
Counting fish.

328
00:13:40,050 --> 00:13:41,950
Then I'll choose Sis to team with me.

329
00:13:43,650 --> 00:13:45,550
Just sit and have a rest.

330
00:13:45,551 --> 00:13:46,900
Mr. He doesn't need a seat.

331
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:49,800
Look, a bug!

332
00:13:49,801 --> 00:13:50,650
Wait, is it a bug?

333
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:52,650
No, it looks like a piece of cauliflower.

334
00:13:54,150 --> 00:13:56,550
It seems that your eyesight is not so good, Sis.

335
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:01,500
Is that ice coffee?

336
00:14:02,150 --> 00:14:03,550
Awesome!

337
00:14:04,750 --> 00:14:06,900
The two strong labors are not here today...

338
00:14:06,901 --> 00:14:08,700
Right, did you notice that two people missing?

339
00:14:08,701 --> 00:14:09,900
Yes.

340
00:14:09,901 --> 00:14:11,550
Peng and

341
00:14:11,551 --> 00:14:12,550
Yixing are not here.

342
00:14:12,551 --> 00:14:13,700
We need two labors,

343
00:14:13,701 --> 00:14:14,700
and you two showed up.

344
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:31,100
What's this music for? A musical play?

345
00:14:31,101 --> 00:14:31,500
Yes.

346
00:14:34,150 --> 00:14:35,450
Show us a solo dance, bro!

347
00:14:38,550 --> 00:14:39,950
The directors are summoning us.

348
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:42,950
Shall we go now?

349
00:14:42,951 --> 00:14:44,050
It's okay. You can take the tea.

350
00:14:48,650 --> 00:14:49,230
I'm a black swan.

351
00:14:49,230 --> 00:14:50,100
The black swan is coming.

352
00:14:51,450 --> 00:14:52,550
What does it mean?

353
00:14:52,551 --> 00:14:53,031
It means an activity.

354
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:53,600
Whenever there are activities,

355
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:54,272
the directors will play this music.

356
00:15:09,550 --> 00:15:12,900
Xixi and the director are wearing suits!

357
00:15:13,792 --> 00:15:14,550
Isn't that our Party A, Wang?

358
00:15:14,551 --> 00:15:15,550
Yes, it is.

359
00:15:15,551 --> 00:15:17,150
Why are you wearing a suit, Wang?

360
00:15:18,150 --> 00:15:19,700
Don't miss it!

361
00:15:19,701 --> 00:15:21,400
Have a look at our goods.

362
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:23,136
Manager Wang.

363
00:15:23,136 --> 00:15:24,906
Manager Wang, right?

364
00:15:24,906 --> 00:15:25,900
Manager Wang.

365
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:27,700
What's this?

366
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:29,900
What does it mean?

367
00:15:30,550 --> 00:15:31,300
In order to help you guys

368
00:15:31,301 --> 00:15:34,100
upgrade from novice fishermen to old fishermen,

369
00:15:34,101 --> 00:15:37,450
we The Shark Group in the north bay

370
00:15:37,451 --> 00:15:39,450
launched a new special offer,

371
00:15:39,451 --> 00:15:40,400
called "Shark Loan".

372
00:15:40,900 --> 00:15:42,950
I was also promoted gloriously

373
00:15:42,951 --> 00:15:44,300
from the captain of "the Shark" to...

374
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:46,550
Credit Manager.

375
00:15:46,551 --> 00:15:47,400
Yes.

376
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:50,300
Have a look at our new business.

377
00:15:50,301 --> 00:15:51,950
What's this?

378
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:54,550
Help novice fishermen move forward warm.

379
00:15:54,551 --> 00:15:56,450
Interest free loan for novice fishermen.

380
00:15:56,451 --> 00:15:58,400
Help you realize fishing freedom in three days,

381
00:15:58,401 --> 00:16:00,300
seafood freedom in seven days.

382
00:16:00,301 --> 00:16:02,050
It's kind of attractive.

383
00:16:02,051 --> 00:16:03,400
This is our previous

384
00:16:03,401 --> 00:16:04,550
success case.

385
00:16:04,551 --> 00:16:05,300
Let me see it.

386
00:16:10,701 --> 00:16:11,800
Why does he look so indecent?

387
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:17,700
But you have to admit that

388
00:16:17,701 --> 00:16:18,021
the other day he caught

389
00:16:18,021 --> 00:16:18,464
a small shark (farmed sharks for market),

390
00:16:18,464 --> 00:16:18,880
and showed it to everyone.

391
00:16:19,456 --> 00:16:20,224
Let me show you that

392
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:23,900
in Shayutang Village,

393
00:16:23,901 --> 00:16:24,550
we caught

394
00:16:24,551 --> 00:16:26,500
a small shark (farmed sharks for market).

395
00:16:26,501 --> 00:16:27,550
This is its mouth.

396
00:16:27,551 --> 00:16:29,200
It's still alive and shaking.

397
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:30,900
That's true.

398
00:16:30,901 --> 00:16:31,550
He really caught it,

399
00:16:31,551 --> 00:16:32,750
a small shark (farmed sharks for market).

400
00:16:32,751 --> 00:16:35,100
You didn't have any tools,

401
00:16:35,101 --> 00:16:36,300
so last time when you went fishing at the sea

402
00:16:36,301 --> 00:16:37,632
you borrowed the net from brother Bo, right?

403
00:16:37,632 --> 00:16:38,450
Right.

404
00:16:38,451 --> 00:16:40,700
Actually there are all sorts of net.

405
00:16:40,701 --> 00:16:42,400
You never catch fish without a proper net.

406
00:16:43,950 --> 00:16:45,200
Let me introduce the nets for you.

407
00:16:46,144 --> 00:16:47,050
There are two kinds of gill net.

408
00:16:47,051 --> 00:16:49,100
They are all for fishing at the sea.

409
00:16:49,101 --> 00:16:51,050
What brother Bo used last time was a gill net.

410
00:16:51,650 --> 00:16:52,100
It was...

411
00:16:52,101 --> 00:16:53,450
We caught a flying fish last time.

412
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:55,700
This is for inshore fishing.

413
00:16:55,701 --> 00:16:57,450
Throw it into the sea and the crabs will catch it.

414
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:00,300
This is for inshore pulling.

415
00:17:00,301 --> 00:17:01,300
You walk into the sea and throw it,

416
00:17:01,301 --> 00:17:02,250
without taking a boat.

417
00:17:03,101 --> 00:17:04,700
Fish cages, you've tried before.

418
00:17:04,701 --> 00:17:05,250
From brother Bo.

419
00:17:05,251 --> 00:17:06,000
Right.

420
00:17:06,050 --> 00:17:06,800
This one is the best.

421
00:17:06,801 --> 00:17:07,850
This is what Xixi used the other day

422
00:17:07,851 --> 00:17:09,150
to catch a small shark (farmed sharks for market).

423
00:17:09,151 --> 00:17:10,250
Light trapping.

424
00:17:10,251 --> 00:17:11,300
For night fishing.

425
00:17:11,301 --> 00:17:11,950
Right.

426
00:17:11,951 --> 00:17:13,150
So these are important tools for you

427
00:17:13,151 --> 00:17:15,050
to convert from poor to rich.

428
00:17:16,100 --> 00:17:18,750
The reason why we caught few seafood last time

429
00:17:18,751 --> 00:17:20,500
is that we didn't have these tools.

430
00:17:20,501 --> 00:17:22,400
Exactly. Last time when you went fishing
with brother Bo,

431
00:17:22,401 --> 00:17:23,900
your harvests were poor, right?

432
00:17:23,901 --> 00:17:25,450
You are backbiting brother Bo.

433
00:17:25,451 --> 00:17:26,500
Does he know it?

434
00:17:27,550 --> 00:17:28,650
Yes.

435
00:17:28,650 --> 00:17:30,300
How come he knows it?

436
00:17:30,301 --> 00:17:30,950
So what are you doing?

437
00:17:30,951 --> 00:17:32,150
Are you selling them?

438
00:17:32,151 --> 00:17:33,250
No, we are offering loans.

439
00:17:33,250 --> 00:17:34,500
How can we get a loan?

440
00:17:34,501 --> 00:17:35,850
You don't have money, right?

441
00:17:38,250 --> 00:17:39,350
You don't have money.

442
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:42,150
We assessed your house.

443
00:17:44,101 --> 00:17:45,350
We can offer you a loan

444
00:17:45,351 --> 00:17:46,950
during your startup.

445
00:17:49,150 --> 00:17:50,350
Here's what I think,

446
00:17:50,351 --> 00:17:50,800
Mr. Huang,

447
00:17:50,801 --> 00:17:53,000
we need the kitchen.

448
00:17:53,001 --> 00:17:53,850
We don't necessarily need the kitchen.

449
00:17:53,851 --> 00:17:54,350
No.

450
00:17:54,351 --> 00:17:55,550
Can we eat outside?

451
00:17:55,551 --> 00:17:56,550
I will not cook.

452
00:17:57,762 --> 00:17:59,200
Let's get RMB 2000 out of it

453
00:17:59,201 --> 00:18:00,600
and get an eel cage.

454
00:18:00,601 --> 00:18:01,800
We can dine with the rest, which is RMB 1200,

455
00:18:02,750 --> 00:18:03,280
right?

456
00:18:03,280 --> 00:18:05,100
This is one way to do it.

457
00:18:05,101 --> 00:18:07,350
We can just get RMB 2000 worth of fish.

458
00:18:08,350 --> 00:18:09,450
No.

459
00:18:09,451 --> 00:18:10,700
We can get rid of the kitchen

460
00:18:10,701 --> 00:18:11,950
and exchange it for money.

461
00:18:11,951 --> 00:18:13,250
The money will be enough for a few days.

462
00:18:13,251 --> 00:18:15,100
The problem is this Shark Loan

463
00:18:15,101 --> 00:18:16,550
won't give you actual money.

464
00:18:16,551 --> 00:18:18,100
It takes your property,

465
00:18:18,101 --> 00:18:19,150
but only gives you tools in return.

466
00:18:19,151 --> 00:18:19,842
Then just take my house

467
00:18:19,842 --> 00:18:20,578
as collateral.

468
00:18:22,950 --> 00:18:23,850
Which one is yours?

469
00:18:23,850 --> 00:18:24,500
Which one of these is yours?

470
00:18:24,501 --> 00:18:26,200
The old man's house.

471
00:18:26,201 --> 00:18:27,101
That's mine.

472
00:18:27,101 --> 00:18:27,950
That's yours?

473
00:18:27,951 --> 00:18:28,850
It depends on our ages.

474
00:18:28,851 --> 00:18:30,000
I'm the oldest here.

475
00:18:30,001 --> 00:18:31,100
Mr. He and I have the old man's house.

476
00:18:31,101 --> 00:18:33,100
Yes. You'll get the

477
00:18:33,101 --> 00:18:34,114
luxury ocean view house

478
00:18:34,114 --> 00:18:34,562
with the teens.

479
00:18:34,562 --> 00:18:36,350
You will live with the teens.

480
00:18:36,351 --> 00:18:38,500
There's an amazing ocean view house up there.

481
00:18:39,750 --> 00:18:40,000
There it is.

482
00:18:40,001 --> 00:18:41,100
Look at that,

483
00:18:41,101 --> 00:18:42,338
the one on the top floor,

484
00:18:42,338 --> 00:18:43,100
That's mine.

485
00:18:47,074 --> 00:18:48,354
What about the balcony?

486
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:49,600
Sure.

487
00:18:49,601 --> 00:18:50,350
We don't need the balcony.

488
00:18:50,351 --> 00:18:51,550
Let's mortgage the balcony.

489
00:18:51,551 --> 00:18:52,600
Okay.

490
00:18:52,601 --> 00:18:53,800
Let's do it.

491
00:18:53,801 --> 00:18:54,800
We'll mortgage the balcony.

492
00:18:54,801 --> 00:18:56,700
Wait, how can I get out of my room then?

493
00:18:56,701 --> 00:18:57,750
Why don't you mortgage my room

494
00:18:57,751 --> 00:18:58,850
and the balcony?

495
00:18:58,851 --> 00:18:59,200
Oh.

496
00:18:59,201 --> 00:18:59,800
He has a point.

497
00:18:59,801 --> 00:19:00,850
I can't get out of my room without the balcony.

498
00:19:00,851 --> 00:19:02,641
Indeed he can't.

499
00:19:02,658 --> 00:19:03,500
True.

500
00:19:03,501 --> 00:19:04,850
How should he get in?

501
00:19:04,851 --> 00:19:05,550
Right.

502
00:19:05,551 --> 00:19:06,350
Hold on.

503
00:19:06,351 --> 00:19:07,750
Uncle Shen can live in the living room.

504
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:09,550
That'll do.

505
00:19:10,350 --> 00:19:11,700
That is the guest's room at the first place.

506
00:19:11,701 --> 00:19:14,200
Honestly, I think we can mortgage both of them.

507
00:19:14,201 --> 00:19:15,000
Alright, we'll mortgage them both.

508
00:19:15,001 --> 00:19:17,200
It's RMB 3000 for them both.

509
00:19:17,201 --> 00:19:19,350
What should we buy with RMB 3000?

510
00:19:19,351 --> 00:19:19,970
How much are these together

511
00:19:19,970 --> 00:19:20,802
for six items?

512
00:19:21,058 --> 00:19:21,762
RMB 2200,

513
00:19:21,762 --> 00:19:23,010
RMB1400,

514
00:19:23,778 --> 00:19:24,194
They total up to RMB 3000.

515
00:19:26,950 --> 00:19:28,600
Give me a discount.

516
00:19:28,601 --> 00:19:30,350
We have to bargain.

517
00:19:30,351 --> 00:19:32,200
RMB 2500 for all of these.

518
00:19:32,201 --> 00:19:32,950
That's not possible.

519
00:19:33,750 --> 00:19:34,600
Please.

520
00:19:34,601 --> 00:19:35,500
I can't.

521
00:19:35,501 --> 00:19:37,050
Let us have RMB 500 of spare money

522
00:19:37,051 --> 00:19:38,350
in case of emergencies,

523
00:19:39,050 --> 00:19:39,350
is that fine?

524
00:19:39,351 --> 00:19:40,550
You can get another loan.

525
00:19:40,551 --> 00:19:41,700
We have nothing left

526
00:19:41,701 --> 00:19:42,300
for another loan.

527
00:19:42,301 --> 00:19:44,050
We have to eat and to live.

528
00:19:44,051 --> 00:19:45,400
Can you take just RMB 2500?

529
00:19:45,401 --> 00:19:47,150
We don't have cash.

530
00:19:47,151 --> 00:19:48,950
I can't give you RMB 500 in cash.

531
00:19:48,951 --> 00:19:49,150
I mean,

532
00:19:49,151 --> 00:19:50,600
just in case,

533
00:19:50,601 --> 00:19:52,050
can you put RMB 500

534
00:19:52,051 --> 00:19:53,800
on our account?

535
00:19:53,801 --> 00:19:54,650
We're friends,

536
00:19:56,770 --> 00:19:57,400
right?

537
00:19:58,400 --> 00:19:58,950
We...

538
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:00,950
Mr. He said RMB 2500.

539
00:20:00,951 --> 00:20:01,850
Awesome.

540
00:20:01,851 --> 00:20:02,921
RMB 2600.

541
00:20:02,921 --> 00:20:03,900
RMB 2500 please.

542
00:20:03,901 --> 00:20:05,350
Here's what I think.

543
00:20:05,351 --> 00:20:05,950
RMB 2500 sounds fair.

544
00:20:05,951 --> 00:20:06,750
Just now

545
00:20:06,751 --> 00:20:08,650
Mr. Shen saw you in stockings.

546
00:20:12,850 --> 00:20:14,550
He's wearing stockings.

547
00:20:14,551 --> 00:20:14,750
Yes.

548
00:20:14,751 --> 00:20:16,950
The sandals are too large.

549
00:20:16,951 --> 00:20:18,450
He's wearing stockings

550
00:20:18,451 --> 00:20:19,450
with huge sandals.

551
00:20:19,451 --> 00:20:21,300
I can't bear watching it.

552
00:20:23,350 --> 00:20:24,150
I feel so bad.

553
00:20:24,151 --> 00:20:25,600
I'm not wearing stockings.

554
00:20:25,601 --> 00:20:26,800
You are.

555
00:20:26,801 --> 00:20:27,900
Did you forget about it?

556
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:31,960
I feel so bad.

557
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:32,800
I can't take it.

558
00:20:32,801 --> 00:20:33,550
He's upset.

559
00:20:33,551 --> 00:20:34,800
Think of the RMB 100

560
00:20:34,801 --> 00:20:35,541
as compensation for damage to mental health.

561
00:20:35,541 --> 00:20:37,350
It makes sense.

562
00:20:39,150 --> 00:20:39,600
Okay?

563
00:20:39,601 --> 00:20:40,194
RMB 2500. Fine.

564
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:41,800
Alright then.

565
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:44,400
If you take a close look,

566
00:20:44,401 --> 00:20:46,150
they're made of cotton.

567
00:20:46,151 --> 00:20:47,150
They're made of cotton,

568
00:20:47,151 --> 00:20:48,150
but he has washed them too many times
that they look like stockings.

569
00:20:48,151 --> 00:20:49,601
Well, they're too thin now.

570
00:20:49,601 --> 00:20:50,550
True.

571
00:20:53,950 --> 00:20:55,450
Sign the contract here.

572
00:20:55,451 --> 00:20:56,381
Sis, go ahead.

573
00:20:56,381 --> 00:20:57,050
Go for it.

574
00:20:57,650 --> 00:20:59,050
If I sign it, we can't take it back.

575
00:20:59,051 --> 00:20:59,600
But if you do it,

576
00:20:59,601 --> 00:21:00,781
you can act like you don't know

577
00:21:00,781 --> 00:21:01,350
You don't know what happened

578
00:21:01,351 --> 00:21:01,800
because you are still young.

579
00:21:01,801 --> 00:21:02,150
Right.

580
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,150
Write the party B

581
00:21:04,450 --> 00:21:05,930
as Family H.

582
00:21:05,930 --> 00:21:06,800
Family H

